==Trivia==
*The ''meta-'' in Metafilibuster draws from its Greek definition, meaning ''beyond'' or ''transcendant'', which indicates an evolved version of [[Filibuster Obstructa]]. However, it could also imply a sequel or continuation, effectively a "post-Filibuster Obstructa".
*Since Filibuster Obstructa resembles [[wikia:dragonball:Frieza|Mecha-Frieza]], Metafilibuster may be a reference to the [[wikia:dragonball:Meta-Cooler|Meta-Coolers]] introduced in ''[[wikia:dragonball:Dragon Ball Z: The Return of Cooler|Dragon Ball Z: The Return of Cooler]]''. This is supported by how Metafilibuster's Japanese description says that his power can change the world and how his first stage's English name is [[A Whole New World]], potentially referencing Meta-Cooler's role as one of the [[wikia:dragonball:Universe Creation Planners|Universe Creation Planners]].
**When unlocked as [[Filibuster Cat X (Special Cat)|Filibuster Cat X]]'s [[True Form]], Metafilibuster takes on a golden hue, which may be a nod to Golden Meta-Cooler.
*Metafilibuster's knockback animation has the hologram glitch slightly. He shares this behavior with his allied counterpart.
*Metafilibuster, [[Super Metal Hippoe]] and [[Firecracker]] are the only enemy units whose knockback animations have multiple frames.
**[[Dark Emperor Nyandam]], [[Director Kurosawah]], [[Skelecat (Enemy)|Skelecat]], [[Gato Amigo (Enemy)|Gato Amigo]], [[Manic Lion Cat (Enemy)|Manic Lion Cat]] and [[The 9th Angel (Enemy)|The 9th Angel]] are all internally set to have knockback animations that last more than 1 frame, however they still remain static when knocked back.
*Metafilibuster's attack cycle is one frame shorter than Filibuster Obstructa's.
*Despite Metafilibuster's English description saying it is immune to all negative effects, it is not immune to Curse, Warp, Toxic and Explosion, although no Cats currently have Toxic or Warp and Curse has no effect on it.
*Metafilibuster has the highest base attack power of all enemies in the game at 3,000,000 damage.

